    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Alex's Skateboarding Webpage\r\n_\"I want to make a webpage about skateboarding because it's my favorite hobby. I want it to feel like two separate parts — history and styles. Both parts should have a color so they look different from the rest of the page.\"_\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/85a4e1573b399af1c11caa0fea2248e3-image-1775016825823.png\" style=\"width: 40%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. Use AI Tutor to build this page step by step. Be specific - name the elements, sizes, colors, and which parts of the page they apply to.\r\n2. Keep prompting until your result is close to Alex's vision. It doesn't need to be identical - just similar enough.\r\n\r\n> **Hint:** Try using `<section>` and `<h2>` tags in HTML, and the `background-color` and `color` properties in CSS. If you're not sure what some of these are: ask AI Tutor!\r\n\r\nWhen you're satisfied with the result, click **Continue**.",
